description:
memory.rs:117-119:

  // json_merge_patch lives in jmap-server (the shared foundation crate).
  // Every reference backend imports it; the canonical RFC 7396 tests live
  // with the function there.

This is wrong. Mail-server's MemoryBackend has its own apply_jmap_patch helper (memory.rs:1057-1063) for the JMAP path-style patch dialect (e.g. 'mailboxIds/abc123'), NOT json_merge_patch. So 'every reference backend imports it' is contradicted by the canonical sibling.

The corrected version: 'json_merge_patch is the RFC 7396 implementation in jmap-server. This backend uses it because Metadata supports flat-key patches. Backends with path-key patch dialect (e.g. jmap-mail-server's Email/set) use a different helper.'

Audience: contributor reading this for the workspace-wide pattern. They will conclude all backends use json_merge_patch and write their own code accordingly.
